1
00:01:27,959 --> 00:01:33,798
WHAT A PHOTO! KYOTO REWIND

2
00:01:41,572 --> 00:01:43,374
Mornin'!

3
00:01:43,608 --> 00:01:44,475
Do you know him?

4
00:01:44,675 --> 00:01:46,944
Yeah, he's a local police officer.

5
00:01:48,146 --> 00:01:50,448
Ah, to be young again.

6
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:56,587
Ugh, not those bossy britches here to complain about something or other again.

7
00:01:57,155 --> 00:01:58,122
-Oh, Ryo-chan. Good morning. -Morning.

8
00:01:58,322 --> 00:01:59,490
Good morning.

9
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:00,691
It's lacking on the drivers' part.

10
00:02:00,925 --> 00:02:05,363
-And last month— -Terai! Don't be so serious.

11
00:02:05,596 --> 00:02:06,364
Huh?

12
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:08,499
Oh, Ryo-san.

13
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:13,938
They're just digging for content for their silly little traffic newsletter.

14
00:02:14,539 --> 00:02:16,974
&lt;i&gt;I was in the men's room&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the other day at HQ.&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:20,411
Figures. No paper when I need it.

16
00:02:20,645 --> 00:02:21,412
Huh?

17
00:02:21,646 --> 00:02:24,482
"GREEN LIGHT"

18
00:02:26,651 --> 00:02:29,053
So can you use softer paper from now on?

19
00:02:29,387 --> 00:02:30,721
How dare you!

20
00:02:30,955 --> 00:02:33,224
We work really hard on those newsletters.

21
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:34,559
You brainless brute!

22
00:02:34,859 --> 00:02:38,496
-That was uncalled for, Ryo-san. -No, it's good for recycling.

23
00:02:38,696 --> 00:02:39,730
You amoeba!

24
00:02:39,964 --> 00:02:42,633
Worse than bacteria or a virus. You're the worst!

25
00:02:43,234 --> 00:02:44,035
Oh, can it!

26
00:02:44,235 --> 00:02:48,839
You should be ticketing cars instead of wasting time on silly newsletters!

27
00:02:49,173 --> 00:02:50,741
You wage thieves!

28
00:02:52,910 --> 00:02:54,979
In a survey aimed at the women...

29
00:02:55,213 --> 00:02:57,448
of the Katsushika Police Department...

30
00:02:58,382 --> 00:03:01,452
-Least marriageable man? Kankichi Ryotsu! -What?

31
00:03:01,686 --> 00:03:04,822
-Least desirable boss? Kankichi Ryotsu! -Huh?

32
00:03:05,022 --> 00:03:08,025
-Least dateable guy? Kankichi Ryotsu! -Why you!

33
00:03:08,226 --> 00:03:13,531
The worst man? The most brutish? The most hopeless? And so on.

34
00:03:13,731 --> 00:03:17,268
The worst in all 17 categories, by a long shot!

35
00:03:17,468 --> 00:03:20,738
Kankichi Ryotsu is the overall worst for six years running!

36
00:03:22,106 --> 00:03:22,907
Congrats.

37
00:03:23,107 --> 00:03:26,744
We'll be publishing these results in the next &lt;i&gt;Green Light&lt;/i&gt;. Enjoy!

38
00:03:27,144 --> 00:03:29,447
Don't you dare! And stop doing that survey!

39
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,748
-Let me go! -Stop it.

40
00:03:30,948 --> 00:03:33,951
Incidentally, most girls want a hug from Nakagawa-san,

41
00:03:34,151 --> 00:03:37,154
and they'd like you to be their brother, Terai-san.

42
00:03:37,388 --> 00:03:38,723
Really?

43
00:03:39,056 --> 00:03:40,024
Damn it...

44
00:03:40,224 --> 00:03:41,425
Well, I'm honored!

45
00:03:41,626 --> 00:03:42,460
For the scoop?

46
00:03:42,693 --> 00:03:44,929
-Come on. Let's get back on topic. -Okay.

47
00:03:45,596 --> 00:03:48,065
-Well, I'm going on patrol. -Where were we?

48
00:03:48,566 --> 00:03:50,801
We were on illegal parking.

49
00:03:51,035 --> 00:03:52,403
Oh, that's right.

50
00:03:52,603 --> 00:03:54,472
Illegal parking is deplorable.

51
00:03:54,705 --> 00:03:56,307
Hmph! You'll regret that.

52
00:03:58,109 --> 00:04:00,444
Ryotsu! What are you doing?

53
00:04:01,412 --> 00:04:02,647
Helping with the interview.

54
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:08,052
Make fun of me, will you? I'll show you everything I've got!

55
00:04:08,819 --> 00:04:12,423
Here, there, and also here. And here too!

56
00:04:12,623 --> 00:04:15,960
This is precisely why you always get voted as the worst, Ryotsu.

57
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,495
That's right!

58
00:04:18,796 --> 00:04:20,731
What about my feelings in all this?

59
00:04:20,965 --> 00:04:22,166
Ryotsu!

60
00:04:22,366 --> 00:04:25,803
I'll prove it's a fair-and-square message straight from me!

61
00:04:26,003 --> 00:04:27,004
Take a picture!

62
00:04:27,772 --> 00:04:28,539
What?

63
00:04:28,773 --> 00:04:30,207
Hurry up! They're coming!

64
00:04:30,641 --> 00:04:31,842
Hmm...

65
00:04:32,076 --> 00:04:33,678
Well then, here goes.

66
00:04:33,911 --> 00:04:34,679
Say cheese!

67
00:04:35,613 --> 00:04:38,316
Goddamn! Quit judging me!

68
00:04:41,152 --> 00:04:45,389
Well, there's nowhere left to go but up once you've hit rock bottom.

69
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:48,125
Thank you for your help.

70
00:04:48,326 --> 00:04:50,528
No, it was my pleasure.

71
00:04:51,128 --> 00:04:52,930
Hey. Done with the interview?

72
00:04:53,364 --> 00:04:54,165
Hmph.

73
00:04:54,365 --> 00:04:56,167
See you two later.

74
00:04:56,634 --> 00:04:58,936
Hey, don't forget your precious camera.

75
00:04:59,403 --> 00:05:01,138
That's not ours.

76
00:05:01,339 --> 00:05:02,173
Hmph!

77
00:05:02,373 --> 00:05:03,240
Huh?

78
00:05:03,974 --> 00:05:05,476
Then whose is it?

79
00:05:05,676 --> 00:05:08,245
Ah, Chief Ohara. Thank you for your hard work.

80
00:05:08,479 --> 00:05:10,948
Uh-oh... Don't tell me it's the Chief's.

81
00:05:11,148 --> 00:05:13,551
&lt;i&gt;Oh, that's my camera, Ryotsu.&lt;/i&gt;

82
00:05:14,118 --> 00:05:15,853
&lt;i&gt;I left it here?&lt;/i&gt;

83
00:05:16,053 --> 00:05:17,888
&lt;i&gt;I've been looking for it.&lt;/i&gt;

84
00:05:20,891 --> 00:05:21,892
&lt;i&gt;Ryotsu?&lt;/i&gt;

85
00:05:22,126 --> 00:05:23,594
&lt;i&gt;What are you going to do?&lt;/i&gt;

86
00:05:23,828 --> 00:05:27,898
&lt;i&gt;I'm going to take a short break.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;You're in charge now, Nakagawa, Reiko.&lt;/i&gt;

87
00:05:28,132 --> 00:05:29,600
&lt;i&gt;Looks like a long break.&lt;/i&gt;

88
00:05:29,834 --> 00:05:31,502
&lt;i&gt;Only five or ten years.&lt;/i&gt;

89
00:05:31,702 --> 00:05:34,572
&lt;i&gt;Ryotsu!&lt;/i&gt;

90
00:05:35,439 --> 00:05:38,409
&lt;i&gt;Is Ryotsu there?&lt;/i&gt;

91
00:05:39,243 --> 00:05:41,612
&lt;i&gt;Chief! What's wrong?&lt;/i&gt;

92
00:05:41,846 --> 00:05:43,381
&lt;i&gt;Ryotsu, where are you going?&lt;/i&gt;

93
00:05:43,581 --> 00:05:46,250
&lt;i&gt;I was just about to go on patrol.&lt;/i&gt;

94
00:05:46,851 --> 00:05:48,753
&lt;i&gt;You stupid moron!&lt;/i&gt;

95
00:05:49,153 --> 00:05:52,757
&lt;i&gt;Go wherever you like, but don't you ever&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;show your face here again!&lt;/i&gt;

96
00:05:53,457 --> 00:05:54,458
&lt;i&gt;You're fired!&lt;/i&gt;

97
00:05:54,692 --> 00:05:56,827
&lt;i&gt;We don't need scum like you!&lt;/i&gt;

98
00:05:57,027 --> 00:05:58,629
&lt;i&gt;No... Chief!&lt;/i&gt;

99
00:05:58,929 --> 00:05:59,864
&lt;i&gt;I can explain—&lt;/i&gt;

100
00:06:01,399 --> 00:06:02,767
&lt;i&gt;You're joking, right?&lt;/i&gt;

101
00:06:03,167 --> 00:06:06,003
&lt;i&gt;I'm not joking. You're fired!&lt;/i&gt;

102
00:06:06,437 --> 00:06:07,538
&lt;i&gt;No!&lt;/i&gt;

103
00:06:07,738 --> 00:06:09,473
&lt;i&gt;Nakagawa, Reiko, help me out!&lt;/i&gt;

104
00:06:09,774 --> 00:06:11,242
-&lt;i&gt;Bye, Ryo-chan.&lt;/i&gt; -&lt;i&gt;So long!&lt;/i&gt;

105
00:06:11,442 --> 00:06:12,243
&lt;i&gt;Huh?&lt;/i&gt;

106
00:06:14,278 --> 00:06:16,747
&lt;i&gt;No! Nakagawa, Reiko!&lt;/i&gt;

107
00:06:16,947 --> 00:06:19,617
&lt;i&gt;How dare you betray me!&lt;/i&gt;

108
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:21,118
&lt;i&gt;Terai!&lt;/i&gt;

109
00:06:21,419 --> 00:06:24,388
&lt;i&gt;Hey, open up!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Open up, or I'll break down this door!&lt;/i&gt;

110
00:06:24,588 --> 00:06:26,924
&lt;i&gt;Don't make me angry now... Huh?&lt;/i&gt;

111
00:06:28,959 --> 00:06:31,462
&lt;i&gt;This cake you made is delicious, Reiko.&lt;/i&gt;

112
00:06:31,662 --> 00:06:33,664
&lt;i&gt;If you like it, there's plenty more.&lt;/i&gt;

113
00:06:34,799 --> 00:06:35,466
&lt;i&gt;Huh?&lt;/i&gt;

114
00:06:36,067 --> 00:06:40,471
&lt;i&gt;Ryo-san. Your bills have been piling up.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;It's time for you to pay us back.&lt;/i&gt;

115
00:06:40,905 --> 00:06:41,972
&lt;i&gt;Wait, please!&lt;/i&gt;

116
00:06:42,206 --> 00:06:44,308
&lt;i&gt;Just wait till my next bonus...&lt;/i&gt;

117
00:06:44,975 --> 00:06:46,944
&lt;i&gt;But if I'm fired, then...&lt;/i&gt;

118
00:06:47,344 --> 00:06:48,512
&lt;i&gt;Pay us back!&lt;/i&gt;

119
00:06:48,746 --> 00:06:53,651
&lt;i&gt;Nakagawa, Reiko, help me!&lt;/i&gt;

120
00:06:54,518 --> 00:06:59,657
Oh, Ryotsu. There it is. That's my camera, so can I have it—

121
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:03,427
C-Chief! This is a good camera.

122
00:07:03,627 --> 00:07:06,464
A Micron F50, no? I've been wanting one of these.

123
00:07:06,664 --> 00:07:07,965
-A solid choice! -Huh?

124
00:07:08,999 --> 00:07:10,434
I'm still not used to it.

125
00:07:10,634 --> 00:07:14,171
I couldn't even figure out the film, and now I'm misplacing it.

126
00:07:15,506 --> 00:07:16,540
Oh really?

127
00:07:18,142 --> 00:07:22,480
I'm glad you found it. To think I left it at the station.

128
00:07:22,713 --> 00:07:23,614
Huh?

129
00:07:23,948 --> 00:07:25,783
He'll be docked pay if he's found out.

130
00:07:25,983 --> 00:07:27,251
Just docked pay?

131
00:07:27,618 --> 00:07:29,487
I want to get it developed, so—

132
00:07:29,687 --> 00:07:31,322
There's no need for that...

133
00:07:31,522 --> 00:07:32,690
Stop this, Ryotsu!

134
00:07:32,923 --> 00:07:34,358
Oh no...

135
00:07:37,828 --> 00:07:39,029
&lt;i&gt;You're joking, right?&lt;/i&gt;

136
00:07:39,497 --> 00:07:42,333
&lt;i&gt;I'm not joking. You're fired!&lt;/i&gt;

137
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,201
Hold on a minute!

138
00:07:44,401 --> 00:07:45,970
Where are you taking them?

139
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:48,305
To the local Pikkari Camera.

140
00:07:48,672 --> 00:07:50,007
No, don't go there.

141
00:07:50,207 --> 00:07:54,812
They charge 20 yen per print. In this day and age! What a fraud.

142
00:07:55,179 --> 00:07:57,414
You know some place cheaper?

143
00:07:57,681 --> 00:08:00,718
Yes! I know a place that doesn't charge for prints.

144
00:08:00,951 --> 00:08:03,387
Don't lie to me. How would they make a profit?

145
00:08:03,587 --> 00:08:05,189
Oh, they do.

146
00:08:05,589 --> 00:08:08,359
A roll of 24 shots costs 600 yen.

147
00:08:08,559 --> 00:08:11,428
Most of the fee goes toward the printing paper.

148
00:08:11,662 --> 00:08:13,564
About 180 yen, or 30%.

149
00:08:13,898 --> 00:08:17,501
Even subtracting 40% for other costs, like chemicals and labor,

150
00:08:17,701 --> 00:08:21,572
that still leaves 30%, or another 180 yen, that gets recorded as profit.

151
00:08:21,906 --> 00:08:23,307
I see, I see.

152
00:08:23,908 --> 00:08:27,178
I need to give the photos to the traffic division tomorrow.

153
00:08:27,378 --> 00:08:28,779
Have them ready by ten.

154
00:08:29,013 --> 00:08:30,047
Leave it to me.

155
00:08:30,247 --> 00:08:32,917
You'll have your photos by 10 a.m., rain or shine!

156
00:08:39,757 --> 00:08:43,360
Shouldn't be too difficult using a color development kit.

157
00:08:43,761 --> 00:08:45,863
I'll just cut out the ones I'm in.

158
00:08:48,465 --> 00:08:50,935
Excuse me, sir. Could we have our ball back?

159
00:08:51,168 --> 00:08:53,437
What are you doing, you little punks!

160
00:08:53,637 --> 00:08:54,638
Run away!

161
00:08:57,641 --> 00:08:58,642
It's ruined!

162
00:09:01,045 --> 00:09:01,812
What?

163
00:09:02,046 --> 00:09:05,049
Well, at least my photos are gone, so that's a success...

164
00:09:05,449 --> 00:09:08,285
But what about the chief's photos?

165
00:09:08,819 --> 00:09:09,653
Hmm...

166
00:09:09,887 --> 00:09:11,655
I think they said it was Kyoto.

167
00:09:11,889 --> 00:09:12,656
What?

168
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:16,227
They said the next newsletter was going to be a photo op-ed

169
00:09:16,427 --> 00:09:19,029
of Chief Ohara's trip to Kyoto.

170
00:09:19,230 --> 00:09:20,064
Are you sure?

171
00:09:20,264 --> 00:09:20,965
Y-Yeah.

172
00:09:21,198 --> 00:09:22,433
Well done, Terai!

173
00:09:22,933 --> 00:09:25,135
Then I can guess what photos he took.

174
00:09:26,203 --> 00:09:30,274
&lt;i&gt;He probably went around Kyoto taking&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;postcard-type photos with nobody in them.&lt;/i&gt;

175
00:09:30,474 --> 00:09:32,476
I'll bet he doesn't even remember.

176
00:09:32,676 --> 00:09:35,079
All I need's some postcard copies and I'm set.

177
00:09:35,279 --> 00:09:37,047
Do you think that'll work?

178
00:09:37,248 --> 00:09:39,583
Don't worry. He'll be none the wiser.

179
00:09:40,150 --> 00:09:40,951
We'll see...

180
00:09:43,053 --> 00:09:45,589
Yes, this is Kameari Park Police Station.

181
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:47,091
&lt;i&gt;Is Ryotsu there?&lt;/i&gt;

182
00:09:48,292 --> 00:09:49,393
&lt;i&gt;Yes, what is it?&lt;/i&gt;

183
00:09:49,593 --> 00:09:50,594
&lt;i&gt;Oh, there you are.&lt;/i&gt;

184
00:09:51,095 --> 00:09:53,464
I meant to say I want silky-finish paper.

185
00:09:53,664 --> 00:09:57,501
I'm standing with the most beautiful maiko in all of Kyoto, after all!

186
00:09:57,701 --> 00:09:59,703
You're standing next to her?

187
00:09:59,937 --> 00:10:03,507
Chief Bonasu from admin took them. They may go in the newsletter.

188
00:10:03,974 --> 00:10:07,344
They're important, so make sure they come out clear and vivid.

189
00:10:07,544 --> 00:10:09,513
&lt;i&gt;O-Okay. Leave it to me.&lt;/i&gt;

190
00:10:11,615 --> 00:10:12,950
Is this it for me?

191
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,885
&lt;i&gt;You're fired!&lt;/i&gt;

192
00:10:15,319 --> 00:10:17,421
A postcard's not gonna cut it.

193
00:10:17,621 --> 00:10:20,991
And people can easily spot bad CG composites these days.

194
00:10:21,992 --> 00:10:23,794
This is your fault! Do something!

195
00:10:23,994 --> 00:10:25,696
It's not my fault!

196
00:10:25,996 --> 00:10:29,800
This is your fault for taking that photo of my face in the first place.

197
00:10:29,999 --> 00:10:31,702
But you told me to.

198
00:10:31,902 --> 00:10:34,571
If I'm getting fired, you're going down with me!

199
00:10:35,005 --> 00:10:37,541
Your short career will be over, Nakagawa.

200
00:10:37,741 --> 00:10:39,343
O-Okay, I'll help you.

201
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,915
-Chief Bonasu! -Yes?

202
00:10:45,816 --> 00:10:47,818
We're going to Kyoto. Right now!

203
00:10:54,725 --> 00:10:56,060
But I'm busy right now?

204
00:10:56,293 --> 00:10:57,494
You're free to go now.

205
00:10:57,695 --> 00:10:59,296
Don't be ridiculous!

206
00:10:59,863 --> 00:11:03,334
You remember the photos you took with Chief Ohara in Kyoto, right?

207
00:11:03,534 --> 00:11:05,736
Yes, that was just last week.

208
00:11:05,936 --> 00:11:09,006
I'm gonna need a clear and vivid reconstruction of them.

209
00:11:09,206 --> 00:11:10,007
O-Okay...

210
00:11:10,607 --> 00:11:11,709
Well, Nakagawa?

211
00:11:11,909 --> 00:11:14,244
I've sent all the data we have on the chief.

212
00:11:14,745 --> 00:11:16,513
Now all we need is his clothing.

213
00:11:18,716 --> 00:11:20,217
Hey, what was he wearing?

214
00:11:20,417 --> 00:11:24,488
Let's see, I think it was a brown suit and a tie.

215
00:11:24,688 --> 00:11:25,489
Okay.

216
00:11:26,857 --> 00:11:27,691
Ah, that's it!

217
00:11:27,891 --> 00:11:28,559
And color?

218
00:11:28,959 --> 00:11:30,227
Let's see...

219
00:11:30,427 --> 00:11:31,862
Clearly and vividly!

220
00:11:32,062 --> 00:11:33,731
This color is close...

221
00:11:34,064 --> 00:11:34,765
Okay.

222
00:11:34,965 --> 00:11:35,866
That's it.

223
00:11:36,066 --> 00:11:36,800
Well done!

224
00:11:37,234 --> 00:11:42,106
My staff are ready and waiting on the ground, so you're good to go.

225
00:11:46,443 --> 00:11:49,880
KYOTO 1:00 P.M.

226
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,415
"YASAKA SHRINE"

227
00:12:01,458 --> 00:12:03,761
Ouch, have we finally arrived?

228
00:12:14,538 --> 00:12:15,806
Chief!

229
00:12:20,778 --> 00:12:22,813
Chief! When did you get here?

230
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:23,947
-Ryotsu. -Huh?

231
00:12:24,648 --> 00:12:27,651
This is a model made from the data we sent just before.

232
00:12:27,851 --> 00:12:28,652
Huh? A model?

233
00:12:29,086 --> 00:12:31,755
See how perfect it is? It even fooled you.

234
00:12:39,029 --> 00:12:41,565
The color and feel are all very well done.

235
00:12:41,765 --> 00:12:43,567
Who'd believe it's only a model?

236
00:12:43,767 --> 00:12:46,270
It's made with SFX-grade foam latex.

237
00:12:46,470 --> 00:12:49,506
You can't tell the difference unless you're up real close.

238
00:12:49,973 --> 00:12:54,511
And the face! Chief gets this nervous look whenever he stands in front of a camera.

239
00:12:54,711 --> 00:12:57,815
But why make something like this?

240
00:12:58,315 --> 00:12:59,783
Don't ask questions!

241
00:12:59,983 --> 00:13:00,951
Ah, but...

242
00:13:01,251 --> 00:13:03,187
Everything's ready, young master.

243
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:06,690
Ryotsu. Our assisting staff have arrived.

244
00:13:06,957 --> 00:13:07,958
Okay.

245
00:13:27,277 --> 00:13:28,812
All of these people?

246
00:13:29,146 --> 00:13:29,913
Yes.

247
00:13:33,817 --> 00:13:34,751
Young master!

248
00:13:35,519 --> 00:13:38,722
We narrowed it down, and it seems this maiko is the one.

249
00:13:39,156 --> 00:13:40,357
Welcome.

250
00:13:40,557 --> 00:13:42,226
It's been a week.

251
00:13:42,459 --> 00:13:44,061
Oh, from the other day!

252
00:13:44,394 --> 00:13:47,197
Okay, the cast is here. Let's begin the photo shoot!

253
00:14:00,944 --> 00:14:01,745
How's this?

254
00:14:02,479 --> 00:14:04,648
The lighting's just right. This is it.

255
00:14:04,848 --> 00:14:06,250
Okay, take the photo!

256
00:14:06,717 --> 00:14:07,784
Ready?

257
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,122
Next is the Kamo River.

258
00:14:18,795 --> 00:14:25,068
Our special effects team also work on computer graphics for blockbuster movies.

259
00:14:25,269 --> 00:14:27,571
Like dinosaur movies and tornado movies?

260
00:14:27,771 --> 00:14:28,438
Exactly.

261
00:14:28,939 --> 00:14:32,342
At this rate, we'll be back at the station by evening.

262
00:14:32,543 --> 00:14:33,944
Thank you for waiting.

263
00:14:34,878 --> 00:14:35,879
Enjoy your meal.

264
00:14:36,079 --> 00:14:37,447
Go on. Eat.

265
00:14:37,681 --> 00:14:41,952
I thought it would be a box lunch. Who knew they'd also have a dining car?

266
00:14:42,152 --> 00:14:44,087
It's standard on location in the US.

267
00:14:48,125 --> 00:14:49,359
This is delicious.

268
00:14:49,793 --> 00:14:55,232
Yes. I recruited the head chef of the Sheraton in Hong Kong.

269
00:14:55,699 --> 00:14:57,968
Where should we put the chief?

270
00:14:58,368 --> 00:15:02,806
Chief Ohara photographed the ducks. He didn't go into the river.

271
00:15:03,006 --> 00:15:05,742
Why didn't you say so? No chief for this one!

272
00:15:05,943 --> 00:15:07,611
I think ducks were flying...

273
00:15:07,811 --> 00:15:09,479
Ducks! Make them fly!

274
00:15:09,713 --> 00:15:10,781
-Yes! -Got it!

275
00:15:13,717 --> 00:15:14,484
Hmm...

276
00:15:14,718 --> 00:15:15,586
What's wrong?

277
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:17,955
They might have been in the water...

278
00:15:18,822 --> 00:15:19,957
Hey, make them swim.

279
00:15:22,292 --> 00:15:23,994
Or maybe they were piggybacking?

280
00:15:25,162 --> 00:15:26,597
Piggyback! Piggyback!

281
00:15:27,931 --> 00:15:28,732
We can't!

282
00:15:28,999 --> 00:15:31,134
Maybe it wasn't ducks...

283
00:15:32,035 --> 00:15:35,439
Pull yourself together! Remember. Clear and vivid.

284
00:15:36,974 --> 00:15:40,477
If you keep pushing him like that, he won't remember anything.

285
00:15:40,844 --> 00:15:44,982
Ah, it was carp! Carp! There were three carp! I'm sure of it!

286
00:15:45,449 --> 00:15:47,117
Carp! Get some carp ready!

287
00:15:56,827 --> 00:15:57,627
How's that?

288
00:15:57,828 --> 00:15:59,363
Yes, it looks fine.

289
00:16:05,135 --> 00:16:06,903
Good! Make it rain!

290
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,514
Turn on the wind!

291
00:16:27,257 --> 00:16:28,792
The chief's flying away!

292
00:16:39,069 --> 00:16:42,172
Okay, just one more. Piece of cake.

293
00:16:48,045 --> 00:16:48,879
Um...

294
00:16:49,079 --> 00:16:51,548
Stop dawdling. Press the shutter.

295
00:16:51,948 --> 00:16:55,419
Well, the winter cherry blossoms were blooming in the background.

296
00:16:55,819 --> 00:16:57,187
Make it bloom!

297
00:16:57,387 --> 00:16:58,188
Got it!

298
00:17:03,727 --> 00:17:06,430
And there were about 50 old folks on a tour.

299
00:17:06,663 --> 00:17:08,198
50 elderly extras!

300
00:17:08,398 --> 00:17:09,266
Okay!

301
00:17:15,105 --> 00:17:17,941
Also, the sunset lit up as far as the eye could see.

302
00:17:18,141 --> 00:17:20,410
You idiot! Don't say that after it's dark!

303
00:17:20,610 --> 00:17:21,411
I'm sorry.

304
00:17:21,945 --> 00:17:23,146
Can we make a sunset?

305
00:17:23,547 --> 00:17:25,849
I don't think so. Not in this darkness.

306
00:17:26,049 --> 00:17:27,417
We'll see what we can do.

307
00:17:51,108 --> 00:17:53,543
This is it! This is the sunset from that day!

308
00:17:53,743 --> 00:17:54,811
Press the shutter!

309
00:17:55,011 --> 00:17:55,812
Okay.

310
00:17:59,082 --> 00:18:00,550
We got everything done.

311
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:01,451
Yeah.

312
00:18:01,985 --> 00:18:04,321
You worked hard too. Good job!

313
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:08,925
There was no need to kick him.

314
00:18:09,126 --> 00:18:14,097
The thought of having two chiefs, even if one is a doll, gives me the creeps.

315
00:18:14,297 --> 00:18:19,336
&lt;i&gt;The train departing from platform 12&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;is the 9:34 Nozomi 304 bound for Tokyo...&lt;/i&gt;

316
00:18:19,569 --> 00:18:21,671
We made it onto the last train of the day.

317
00:18:22,272 --> 00:18:24,641
And we'll arrive in Tokyo before midnight.

318
00:18:24,841 --> 00:18:27,644
I'll develop the film when I get home. Now we relax.

319
00:18:27,844 --> 00:18:28,645
Ah!

320
00:18:29,913 --> 00:18:30,680
What is it?

321
00:18:31,047 --> 00:18:33,450
There was one more photo.

322
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:34,451
What?

323
00:18:34,785 --> 00:18:37,854
The most important photo. The one of the Buddha statue.

324
00:18:38,054 --> 00:18:39,389
Wait! Wait!

325
00:18:41,925 --> 00:18:43,860
Yes. Yes, I understand.

326
00:18:44,494 --> 00:18:48,598
No good. The film crew have all just left for a shoot in Alaska.

327
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:49,833
What about our ride?

328
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,769
It's in Nagoya for engine repairs.

329
00:18:52,969 --> 00:18:54,838
It'll be out for a few hours.

330
00:18:55,038 --> 00:18:58,842
Damn... Looks like I'll have to take the photo on my own.

331
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:02,345
Ryotsu! Did you find it?

332
00:19:06,783 --> 00:19:10,020
Just how much more trouble are you gonna cause me?

333
00:19:14,191 --> 00:19:16,226
Ryotsu! Are you okay?

334
00:19:18,628 --> 00:19:22,732
Open up! Open the gate! Show me the Buddha statue!

335
00:19:22,966 --> 00:19:24,267
Open up! Hey!

336
00:19:25,735 --> 00:19:28,271
The statue looks a bit like Ryotsu, doesn't it?

337
00:19:28,505 --> 00:19:30,574
This is no ordinary Buddha statue.

338
00:19:31,007 --> 00:19:34,211
It's only ever shown once every thousand years for three minutes.

339
00:19:34,411 --> 00:19:36,847
It's a super national treasure.

340
00:19:37,047 --> 00:19:37,981
Let me see it!

341
00:19:38,181 --> 00:19:39,849
What is it? It's very late.

342
00:19:40,050 --> 00:19:41,585
Show me this Buddha statue!

343
00:19:41,818 --> 00:19:43,720
That's only once every thousand—

344
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,422
Don't be so stingy!

345
00:19:45,856 --> 00:19:48,191
You disrespectful swine!

346
00:19:53,363 --> 00:19:54,397
Are you okay?

347
00:19:54,598 --> 00:19:58,702
Ugh... Damn it! I'll just have to sneak in then.

348
00:20:08,612 --> 00:20:11,414
Ryotsu, we really shouldn't be doing this.

349
00:20:11,615 --> 00:20:13,450
Isn't this trespassing?

350
00:20:13,683 --> 00:20:15,252
Who cares right now?

351
00:20:15,452 --> 00:20:17,153
Who is it? Who's there?

352
00:20:17,387 --> 00:20:18,288
Ryotsu!

353
00:20:18,488 --> 00:20:19,322
What do we do?

354
00:20:19,556 --> 00:20:20,857
Run away!

355
00:20:40,277 --> 00:20:42,412
Security is too tight. It's impossible.

356
00:20:42,612 --> 00:20:44,614
You're telling me to give up now?

357
00:20:44,981 --> 00:20:48,818
No, but we won't be able to see it for another thousand years...

358
00:20:49,052 --> 00:20:49,819
Ah!

359
00:20:50,053 --> 00:20:52,722
What? You got an idea?

360
00:20:52,922 --> 00:20:54,925
Oh yeah! That should work!

361
00:20:55,125 --> 00:20:55,892
Yes!

362
00:20:56,092 --> 00:20:58,728
What is it? Huh? Huh?

363
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:16,980
Damn you... Why's it gotta be me?

364
00:21:17,347 --> 00:21:18,615
Amazing...

365
00:21:18,815 --> 00:21:20,483
You look like twins, Ryotsu!

366
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:21,751
I do?

367
00:21:23,186 --> 00:21:24,087
No time to waste.

368
00:21:25,488 --> 00:21:27,023
Let's get this over with.

369
00:21:27,490 --> 00:21:31,561
First, turn around, twist your body, and face this way.

370
00:21:32,862 --> 00:21:33,830
Like this?

371
00:21:34,331 --> 00:21:37,534
The statue's right arm goes behind its neck to its left cheek,

372
00:21:37,767 --> 00:21:39,869
and its fingers are in its mouth.

373
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:42,138
Like this?

374
00:21:42,339 --> 00:21:46,509
Its legs are also crossed, and it's standing on one big toe.

375
00:21:48,979 --> 00:21:53,350
The left arm is pointing from the inside of the crossed legs toward the nostrils.

376
00:21:53,550 --> 00:21:56,720
The right eye looks northeast, and the left eye looks southwest.

377
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,956
Hurry up and take the picture!

378
00:22:00,423 --> 00:22:01,524
Okay, I'll take it.

379
00:22:12,869 --> 00:22:14,404
Can I make it?

380
00:22:24,047 --> 00:22:26,016
Ryo-chan's still not back yet.

381
00:22:26,216 --> 00:22:27,083
You're right.

382
00:22:27,283 --> 00:22:28,084
Oh!

383
00:22:28,284 --> 00:22:30,086
Hey, is Ryotsu here?

384
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:31,921
Well, you see...

385
00:22:32,155 --> 00:22:34,424
What? You gave him the wrong camera?

386
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:36,860
So it would seem.

387
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:42,866
I added film, but decided it was too heavy at the last minute and took this instead.

388
00:22:43,066 --> 00:22:44,267
I see...

389
00:22:44,467 --> 00:22:45,902
Chief!

390
00:22:46,102 --> 00:22:46,903
Oh!

391
00:22:47,404 --> 00:22:48,471
They're done!

392
00:22:52,008 --> 00:22:54,611
Chief, the photos are ready.

393
00:22:54,844 --> 00:22:56,479
Is that Ryotsu?

394
00:22:56,713 --> 00:22:57,547
Ryo-chan?

395
00:22:57,747 --> 00:22:58,748
What a getup!

396
00:22:59,082 --> 00:23:01,951
Here, look. These are your photos.

397
00:23:02,185 --> 00:23:03,219
My photos?

398
00:23:04,721 --> 00:23:05,622
What the heck?

399
00:23:09,192 --> 00:23:10,427
There's two of me...

400
00:23:10,627 --> 00:23:12,262
Why do you already have these?

401
00:23:12,462 --> 00:23:14,631
It's identical, right down to the pose.

402
00:23:14,931 --> 00:23:17,600
But the finer details are a little different...

403
00:23:17,934 --> 00:23:21,337
What is this? What are you up to this time, Ryotsu?

404
00:23:21,638 --> 00:23:23,773
It's not like that, Chief!

405
00:23:25,241 --> 00:23:27,043
There it is! The photo of the day!

406
00:23:27,243 --> 00:23:29,345
Enjoy the next issue of &lt;i&gt;Green Light&lt;/i&gt;.

407
00:23:29,746 --> 00:23:31,247
Damn you!

408
00:23:33,917 --> 00:23:35,118
Get back here!

409
00:23:35,318 --> 00:23:38,655
Now, let's hear this explanation in full, Ryotsu.

410
00:23:38,888 --> 00:23:43,226
Chief! Wait! There's a good reason for this...

411
00:23:43,426 --> 00:23:45,328
"CHIEF OHARA'S KYOTO TRAVELOGUE"

412
00:23:46,763 --> 00:23:49,599
"THE WORST MAN OF 1996 KANKICHI RYOTSU BECOMES A MONK"

413
00:23:53,436 --> 00:23:55,705
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

414
00:23:55,939 --> 00:24:02,078
100 MILLION YEN FOR A PHOTO SHOOT, ONE BICYCLE
